--
-- PostGIS values and history: the same table built different ways has one
-- root hash; rewrites that change only how a value is stored show no
-- change; merges combine disjoint spatial edits and conflict on different
-- bytes (spatially equal or not); geometry keys order, merge and refuse
-- as they should.
--
\set ECHO none
on main|t
one root for one table|t|7
checkout|t
rewritten: no change|t
stored uncompressed: no change|t
same root after|t
root unchanged|t
three moved|t
diff: exactly the moved rows|modified:1,modified:39,modified:101
checkout main|t
mg base|t
branch|t
mg main|t
checkout side|t
mg side|t
spatially equal|t
merge|{0,1,"conflicts found"}
conflicts|8:POINT(-2 -2)|POINT(-1 -1), 9:POLYGON((1 0,1 1,0 0,1 0))|POLYGON((0 0,1 0,1 1,0 0))
resolve theirs|t
merged|t
disjoint edits both kept|1:POINT(1 101),5:POINT(5 105),6:POINT(6 6),11:POINT(111 11),15:POINT(115 15),16:POINT(16 16)
same polygon kept|16001|t
conflicts resolved|8:POINT(-1 -1),9:POLYGON((0 0,1 0,1 1,0 0))
checkout main|t
keys|t
branch|t
keys main|t
checkout keys|t
keys side|t
merge keys|{0,0,"merge successful"}
heap copy|t
merged keys in heap order|t|180
composite keys merged|28|29
merged keys|t
side violations|t
checkout main|t
main violations|t
checkout keys|t
merge violating|{0,1,"conflicts found"}
violations|public.gis_ex 1, public.gis_uq 1
unique violation|unique index
exclusion violation|unique index
nothing merged|2|2
long key|54000 primary key of 128035 bytes exceeds the maximum 32724 for prolly table "gis_pk"
checkout main|t
